WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.972
Welcome to Module 10.

00:00:01.972 --> 00:00:10.517
We are now moving from general Python and numerical work into one of the most useful tools for practical data analysis:

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:11.912
Pandas.

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:21.232
Pandas helps us work with table-shaped data, where each row represents an observation and each column represents a

00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:27.522
variable. Throughout this module, we will follow the same workflow analysts use in real projects.

00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:34.747
We will load data, inspect it, identify quality problems, clean and transform columns, summarize groups,

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:38.372
combine related tables, and validate the final result.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:44.402
The goal is not to memorize every Pandas function.

00:00:44.402 --> 00:00:50.458
The goal is to become comfortable solving common data problems in a clear and repeatable way.

00:00:51.106 --> 00:00:56.408
As you work through the examples, pay attention to the reasoning behind each step.

00:00:56.408 --> 00:01:01.098
A successful analysis is not just code that runs.

00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:06.632
It is a process that produces data you understand and results you can explain.
